      "observed": "C2 is only 100pF and is the sole capacitor shown from the LM1117-5.0 output rail to ground.",
      "expected": "The LM1117 output should have an appropriately sized output capacitor; typical LM1117 applications require capacitance on the order of 10µF for stable regulation, rather than 100pF.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "C2 | 100pF | Capacitor_SMD:C_0805_2012Metric | Device:C_Small"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "+5V : C2.1(passive) ... U1.2(VO,power_out)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "GND : C2.2(passive) ..."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Insufficient output capacitance can make the regulator unstable or poorly respond to load transients, potentially disturbing the +5V rail and the MCU supply.",
      "confidence": 0.82
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist ties two separate MCU outputs and their control/programming pins together without a selection mechanism, creating a credible contention risk. The LM1117 output also appears to have only a 100pF capacitor, far below typical output-capacitance requirements."
}

